{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076290-obrimos-legacies","id":1076290,"title":"Obrimos Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-10T21:47:26-07:00","id":1076290,"title":"Obrimos Legacies","content":"Does anyone know of any good Obrimos Legacies? Or, if not, how do you create your own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There was a signature here. It's gone now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8730-pandorym","name":"Pandorym","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8730_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:49:04-07:00","id":1076293,"title":"","content":"I personally like Thrice-Great and Eyes of Ain-Soph, but I'm sure there are even cooler ones I don't know about. I might be getting them wrong though and they're not Obrimos? But I think they are...<br /> EDIT:<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Legacy_(MTAw\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Legacy_(MTAw</a>)<br /> <br /> This will get you started, it will let you browse the basic concept of the legacies and then look them up in their appropriate books. If you do not have those books then their descriptions would let you get started on updating them for your own needs. Any that you are interested in but don't know if you can update yourself, 21C Hermit has a thread where they've been homebrewing updates for the legacies that you can check out and see.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you probably will need to update them, unless you're playing 1E. Last I heard, the developers weren't going to try and update everything because they wanted the &quot;list-of-things&quot; books to not become obsolete after 2E, so we won't be seeing a legacy book for awhile or something like that. Assuming that holds true I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 04-11-2017, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:24:05-07:00","id":1076326,"title":"","content":"I know they're Left-Handed, but the Echo Walkers are really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:38:04-07:00","id":1076333,"title":"","content":"To create an Obrimos Legacy, remember that the Path of Might is about Power and Command. The Obrimos are bringers and shapers of order, enabled by wielding Power and Commanding stuff to be orderly. If the concept you have for a potential homebrew Legacy doesn't fit into that logic, then other Paths might be better.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the Perfected Adepts. They have a clear focus, and can cover both philosophical contemplations about the cosmos and kicking ass with magic kung-fu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T04:55:46-07:00","id":1076412,"title":"","content":"There are a bunch of fantastic ones, many of which I've converted to 2e.<br /> My personal favorites are the Thrice-Great and the Ascended Adepts.<br /> <br /> Thrice-Great are Mages who believe that the ptomelaic model of the solar system is in fact a ladder of spiritual rungs to the Supernal, who if you can attune yourself to each of their Spirit Courts, you can follow the path your Legacy's creator laid down into Ascension. Drawing upon the symbology of those planets and their courts to enhance your magic in the meantime. They're a great legacy who shows how some Mages cling desperately to anachronisms, and how some objectively wrong formulas can still have power if you believe in them.<br /> <br /> The Ascended Adepts are fantastic because their focus on the Mind Arcanum is so simple, but so different from most other Legacy's perspective. But also because they're a quite intensive Legacy that influences its members in a very large way without going Left Handed. Also I like the thought of a community of ascetic Mages who communicate mind-to-mind constantly. Perhaps exploring the limits of consciousness and the Astral.<br /> <br /> Both of which I've updated to 2e.<br /> I also like the Daksha too, because they're hilariously ignorant of the ludicrous nature of their own history and claim Atlantean heritage with a straight face.<br /> Also because they're a nice &quot;oh hey, the Pentacle can be super racist too&quot; group in the modern era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T11:17:59-07:00","id":1076594,"title":"","content":"I've made two Obrimos legacies for 2e, both with a tech/Free Council bent.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889501-2e-legacy-mentats\">The Mentats,</a> a legacy hearkening to the discipline from <i>Dune</i>, focused on human-computing with a sigint twist; and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">Thaumatech Engineers</a>, who seek to inspire Sleepers and bring the Supernal ever closer to the Phenomenal through reverse engineering magical items.<br /> <br /> I think the easiest way to start is to use top-down design: first come up with the flavor and then figure out the mechanics afterward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-11-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}